        <briefdescription>
<para>Submits <computeroutput>body</computeroutput> to a <ref refid="classDbExecutor" kindref="compound">DbExecutor</ref>, answering 503 if it cannot be accepted. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Wraps runOnExecutor with the database-busy message. The callback is shared with the queued task so it remains available for the 503 reply if submission fails. Any database work that must not run on an IO thread belongs in <computeroutput>body</computeroutput>. <parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Body</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Callable taking a <computeroutput><ref refid="callback_8hpp_1a46d97763fde9c175df21fc9b8f73b1d3" kindref="member">CALLBACK_</ref></computeroutput> by value/rvalue reference. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">executor</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Executor that runs the body. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">callback</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Completion callback invoked with (status, message). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">body</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Work to run on a worker; not invoked when the queue is full. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="post"><para>Exactly one of <computeroutput>body</computeroutput> (on a worker) or <computeroutput>callback</computeroutput> with 503 (on the caller) runs. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
