    <briefdescription>
<para>BoundedExecutor configured for the synchronous database path. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This header declares <ref refid="classDbExecutor" kindref="compound">DbExecutor</ref>, a thin subclass of BoundedExecutor that runs blocking database work off the Drogon IO threads. It has two constructors: one takes worker count, queue size and fast-path flag from configuration, the other takes explicit sizes for tests. It also provides <ref refid="dbexecutor_8hpp_1a936968e57939fceaf59b5600a46630aa" kindref="member">runOnDbExecutor()</ref>, a helper that submits work and answers 503 itself if the bounded queue is full.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: Drogon&apos;s IO threads must stay free to accept and route HTTP requests; a slow SQL query on one of them would stall every other request. Routes obtain the shared <ref refid="classDbExecutor" kindref="compound">DbExecutor</ref> from the <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref> and call <ref refid="dbexecutor_8hpp_1a936968e57939fceaf59b5600a46630aa" kindref="member">runOnDbExecutor()</ref> so permission checks, queries and response building run on dedicated workers. The optional IO-thread fast path (see <ref refid="dbprobe_8hpp" kindref="compound">dbprobe.hpp</ref>) lets requests that need no database finish without ever queueing. Without this executor, blocking database work would run on IO threads and the server would grind to a halt under load.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Inheritance / derived classes: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/derived_class">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/derived_class</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Function templates: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/function_template">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/function_template</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Perfect forwarding (std::forward): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/forward">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/forward</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::size_t (an unsigned size type): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/size_t">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/size_t</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Thread pools and bounded queues (back-pressure)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
